# Static Site Generation (SSG) ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

## 🤯 Problem

Your School's "About Us" page

NEVER changes — same content for months.

Re-generating its HTML on the server for EVERY single visitor

is wasted work, when the content is identical every time.

---

## 🧠 Think Like This

Imagine PRE-PRINTING 10,000 copies

of a School Brochure ONCE,

instead of re-typing and re-printing

a fresh copy EVERY time someone asks for one.

Static Generation builds the page ONCE, at build time,

then serves that SAME pre-built HTML to everyone, instantly.

---

## ✅ What is it?

Static Site Generation builds a page's HTML

ONCE, at BUILD TIME (when you deploy),

rather than on every request.

That pre-built HTML is served instantly from a CDN

to every visitor.

---

## 🤔 Why do we use it?

The FASTEST possible page load — no server work happens per request at all.

Perfect for content that rarely changes

(About pages, blog posts, documentation).

---

## 🧠 Never Forget This

🖨 Pre-Printed Brochures

Built ONCE, served MANY times, instantly, to everyone.

---

## 💼 Real Project

School ERP

The public "About the School" and "Admission Process" pages

rarely change — perfect candidates for Static Generation.

They load INSTANTLY for every visitor,

with zero server computation per request.

---

## ⚠ Interview Trap

❌ Using Static Generation for FREQUENTLY-changing data

(like live attendance records or today's announcements).

That data would stay STALE

until the next deployment/rebuild —

use SSR or ISR instead for frequently-changing content.

---

## 💻 Pattern

```jsx
// app/about/page.js — Server Component, statically generated by default
// (no dynamic data fetching, no cache: 'no-store' → Next.js generates it once at build time)
export default function AboutPage() {
    return <h1>About Our School</h1>;
}
```

```jsx
// With static data fetching (cached indefinitely by default)
async function AboutPage() {
    const data = await fetch('https://api.example.com/about'); // cached, built once
    return <p>{data.description}</p>;
}
```

---

## 🔄 Angular Brain

Similar to Angular Universal's

"prerendering" feature —

generating fully static HTML files at BUILD time

for routes that don't need per-request server logic.

---

## 🎤 Interview Answer

Static Site Generation pre-builds a page's HTML once at build time, rather than on every request, and serves that same static file instantly to every visitor, often from a CDN. It's ideal for content that rarely changes, like marketing or informational pages, offering the fastest possible load time since no per-request rendering work is needed.

---

## 📝 Keywords

SSG

Static Generation

Build Time

CDN

Pre-rendering

